{"chunk": 0, "n": 1, "rules": [{"quote": "If there is no snow before January, there will be the more in March and April.", "cond": {"start": "12-01", "end": "12-31", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "03-01", "end": "04-30", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}}]}
{"chunk": 1, "n": 2, "rules": [{"quote": "March in Janiveer, Janiveer in March, I fear.", "cond": {"start": "01-01", "end": "01-31", "var": "temp", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "03-01", "end": "03-31", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}}, {"quote": "A warm January, a cold May.", "cond": {"start": "01-01", "end": "01-31", "var": "temp", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "05-01", "end": "05-31", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}}]}
{"chunk": 2, "n": 0, "rules": []}
{"chunk": 3, "n": 1, "rules": [{"quote": "If St. Paul's Day be fine, the year will be the same.", "cond": {"start": "01-25", "end": "01-25", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "01-25", "end": "01-24", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}}]}
{"chunk": 4, "n": 0, "rules": []}
{"chunk": 5, "n": 0, "rules": []}
{"chunk": 6, "n": 2, "rules": [{"quote": "February fill dyke; March lick it out.", "cond": {"start": "02-01", "end": "02-28", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "03-01", "end": "03-31", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}}, {"quote": "If February give much snow, a fine summer it doth foreshow.", "cond": {"start": "02-01", "end": "02-28", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "06-01", "end": "08-31", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}}]}
{"chunk": 7, "n": 3, "rules": [{"quote": "Whenever the latter part of February and beginning of March are dry, there will be a deficiency of rain up to Midsummer Day.", "cond": {"start": "02-15", "end": "03-10", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "03-10", "end": "06-24", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}}, {"quote": "For every thunder with rain in February there will be a cold spell in May.", "cond": {"start": "02-01", "end": "02-28", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "05-01", "end": "05-31", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}}, {"quote": "As long as the sunbeam comes in on Bridget's feast-day, the snow comes before May Day.", "cond": {"start": "02-01", "end": "02-01", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "02-01", "end": "05-01", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}}]}
{"chunk": 8, "n": 1, "rules": [{"quote": "If Marie's purifying dale be cleare and bright with sunnie raie, then frost and cold shall be much more after the feast.", "cond": {"start": "02-02", "end": "02-02", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "02-03", "end": "03-31", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}}]}
{"chunk": 9, "n": 10, "rules": [{"quote": "As far as the sun shines in on Candlemas Day, So far will the snow blow in afore old May.", "cond": {"start": "02-02", "end": "02-02", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "02-02", "end": "05-13", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}}, {"quote": "Should the sun shine out at the Purification, there will be more ice after the festival than there was before it.", "cond": {"start": "02-02", "end": "02-02", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "02-02", "end": "03-25", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}}, {"quote": "When on the Purification the sun hath shined, The greater part of winter comes behind.", "cond": {"start": "02-02", "end": "02-02", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "02-02", "end": "03-25", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}}, {"quote": "As far as the sun shines in at the window on Candlemas Day, so deep will the snow be ere winter is gone.", "cond": {"start": "02-02", "end": "02-02", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "02-02", "end": "03-25", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}}, {"quote": "On Candlemas Day, just so far as the sun shines in, just so far will the snow blow in.", "cond": {"start": "02-02", "end": "02-02", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "02-02", "end": "03-25", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}}, {"quote": "If Candlemas Day be fair and bright, Winter will have another flight.", "cond": {"start": "02-02", "end": "02-02", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "02-02", "end": "03-25", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}}, {"quote": "If Candlemas Day bring clouds and rain, Winter is gone and won't come again.", "cond": {"start": "02-02", "end": "02-02", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "02-02", "end": "03-25", "var": "temp", "dir": "above"}}, {"quote": "If Candlemas Day be stormy and black It carries the winter away on its back.", "cond": {"start": "02-02", "end": "02-02", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "02-02", "end": "03-25", "var": "temp", "dir": "above"}}, {"quote": "Good weather on this day indicates a long continuance of winter. \u2014 Isle of Man.", "cond": {"start": "02-02", "end": "02-02", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "02-02", "end": "03-25", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}}, {"quote": "On the contrary, if foul it is a good omen. \u2014 Isle of Man.", "cond": {"start": "02-02", "end": "02-02", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "02-02", "end": "03-25", "var": "temp", "dir": "above"}}]}
{"chunk": 10, "n": 5, "rules": [{"quote": "If Candlemas Day be dry and fair, the half of the winter's to come and mair.", "cond": {"start": "02-02", "end": "02-02", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "02-02", "end": "03-25", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}}, {"quote": "If Candlemas Day be wet and foul, the half of the winter is gone at Yule.", "cond": {"start": "02-02", "end": "02-02", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "02-02", "end": "03-25", "var": "temp", "dir": "above"}}, {"quote": "After Candlemas Day the frost will be more keen, if the sun then shines bright, than before it has been.", "cond": {"start": "02-02", "end": "02-02", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "02-02", "end": "03-25", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}}, {"quote": "If a storm on February 2nd, spring is near.", "cond": {"start": "02-02", "end": "02-02", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "02-02", "end": "03-01", "var": "temp", "dir": "above"}}, {"quote": "If that day be bright and clear, the spring will be late.", "cond": {"start": "02-02", "end": "02-02", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "02-02", "end": "04-01", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}}]}
{"chunk": 11, "n": 2, "rules": [{"quote": "When drops hang on the fence on February 2nd, icicles will hang thereon March 25th.", "cond": {"start": "02-02", "end": "02-02", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "03-25", "end": "03-25", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}}, {"quote": "If the eighteen last days of February be wet, and the first ten of March, the spring quarter and summer too will prove too wet.", "cond": {"start": "02-11", "end": "03-10", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "03-25", "end": "09-29", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}}]}
{"chunk": 12, "n": 3, "rules": [{"quote": "If cold at St. Peter's Day, it will last longer (shows weather for next forty days).", "cond": {"start": "02-22", "end": "02-22", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "02-22", "end": "04-03", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}}, {"quote": "If it freezes on St. Matthias' Day, it will freeze for a month together.", "cond": {"start": "02-24", "end": "02-24", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "02-24", "end": "03-24", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}}, {"quote": "St. Matthias breaks the ice; if he finds none, he will make it.", "cond": {"start": "02-24", "end": "02-24", "var": "temp", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "02-24", "end": "03-24", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}}]}
{"chunk": 13, "n": 0, "rules": []}
{"chunk": 14, "n": 0, "rules": []}
{"chunk": 15, "n": 0, "rules": []}
{"chunk": 16, "n": 2, "rules": [{"quote": "March comes in like a lion and goes out like a lamb.", "cond": {"start": "03-01", "end": "03-10", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "03-21", "end": "03-31", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}}, {"quote": "March comes in like a lamb and goes out like a lion.", "cond": {"start": "03-01", "end": "03-10", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "03-21", "end": "03-31", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}}]}
{"chunk": 17, "n": 1, "rules": [{"quote": "So many frosts in March, so many in May.", "cond": {"start": "03-01", "end": "03-31", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "05-01", "end": "05-31", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}}]}
{"chunk": 18, "n": 1, "rules": [{"quote": "As it rains in March, so it rains in June.", "cond": {"start": "03-01", "end": "03-31", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "06-01", "end": "06-30", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}}]}
{"chunk": 19, "n": 0, "rules": []}
{"chunk": 20, "n": 0, "rules": []}
{"chunk": 21, "n": 0, "rules": []}
{"chunk": 22, "n": 1, "rules": [{"quote": "High winds on these days [borrowing days, late March], a dry summer to follow", "cond": {"start": "03-29", "end": "04-01", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "06-01", "end": "08-31", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}}]}
{"chunk": 23, "n": 0, "rules": []}
{"chunk": 24, "n": 0, "rules": []}
{"chunk": 25, "n": 2, "rules": [{"quote": "After a wet April a dry June.", "cond": {"start": "04-01", "end": "04-30", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "06-01", "end": "06-30", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}}, {"quote": "Moist April, clear June.", "cond": {"start": "04-01", "end": "04-30", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "06-01", "end": "06-30", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}}]}
{"chunk": 26, "n": 2, "rules": [{"quote": "If the first three days of April be foggy, there will be a flood in June.", "cond": {"start": "04-01", "end": "04-03", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "06-01", "end": "06-30", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}}, {"quote": "If the first three days in April be foggy, Rain in June will make the lanes boggy.", "cond": {"start": "04-01", "end": "04-03", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "06-01", "end": "06-30", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}}]}
{"chunk": 27, "n": 0, "rules": []}
{"chunk": 28, "n": 0, "rules": []}
{"chunk": 29, "n": 0, "rules": []}
{"chunk": 30, "n": 0, "rules": []}
{"chunk": 31, "n": 0, "rules": []}
{"chunk": 32, "n": 1, "rules": [{"quote": "A dry May is followed by a wet June.", "cond": {"start": "05-01", "end": "05-31", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "06-01", "end": "06-30", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}}]}
{"chunk": 33, "n": 0, "rules": []}
{"chunk": 34, "n": 3, "rules": [{"quote": "Wet May, dry July.", "cond": {"start": "05-01", "end": "05-31", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "07-01", "end": "07-31", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}}, {"quote": "If May be cold and wet, September will be warm and dry, and vice-versa.", "cond": {"start": "05-01", "end": "05-31", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "09-01", "end": "09-30", "var": "temp", "dir": "above"}}, {"quote": "If May be cold and wet, September will be warm and dry, and vice-versa.", "cond": {"start": "05-01", "end": "05-31", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "09-01", "end": "09-30", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}}]}
{"chunk": 35, "n": 1, "rules": [{"quote": "Storms from the east or south-east, between 17th and 23rd of March, indicate a wet summer.", "cond": {"start": "03-17", "end": "03-23", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "06-01", "end": "08-31", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}}]}
{"chunk": 36, "n": 5, "rules": [{"quote": "A wet June makes a dry September.", "cond": {"start": "06-01", "end": "06-30", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "09-01", "end": "09-30", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}}, {"quote": "If it rain on June 8th (St. Medard), it will rain forty days later.", "cond": {"start": "06-08", "end": "06-08", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "06-09", "end": "07-18", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}}, {"quote": "If it rain on June 19th (St. Protais), it rains for forty days after.", "cond": {"start": "06-19", "end": "06-19", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "06-20", "end": "07-29", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}}, {"quote": "If St. Vitus's Day be rainy weather, it will rain for thirty days together.", "cond": {"start": "06-15", "end": "06-15", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "06-16", "end": "07-15", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}}, {"quote": "When it is hottest in June, it will be coldest in the corresponding days of the next February.", "cond": {"start": "06-01", "end": "06-30", "var": "temp", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "02-01", "end": "02-28", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}}]}
{"chunk": 37, "n": 0, "rules": []}
{"chunk": 38, "n": 1, "rules": [{"quote": "If it rains on June 27th, it will rain seven weeks.", "cond": {"start": "06-27", "end": "06-27", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "06-27", "end": "08-15", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}}]}
{"chunk": 39, "n": 6, "rules": [{"quote": "If the 1st of July it be rainy weather, It will rain more or less for four weeks together.", "cond": {"start": "07-01", "end": "07-01", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "07-01", "end": "07-29", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}}, {"quote": "If it rains on St. Mary's Day, it will rain for four weeks.", "cond": {"start": "07-02", "end": "07-02", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "07-02", "end": "07-30", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}}, {"quote": "If it rains on first dog-day, it will rain for forty days after.", "cond": {"start": "07-03", "end": "07-03", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "07-03", "end": "08-12", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}}, {"quote": "Bullion's Day, gif ye be fair, For forty days 'twill rain nae mair.", "cond": {"start": "07-04", "end": "07-04", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "07-04", "end": "08-13", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}}, {"quote": "If it rains on July 10th, it will rain for seven weeks.", "cond": {"start": "07-10", "end": "07-10", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "07-10", "end": "08-28", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}}, {"quote": "When the months of July, August, and September are unusually hot, January will be the coldest month.", "cond": {"start": "07-01", "end": "09-30", "var": "temp", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "01-01", "end": "01-31", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}}]}
{"chunk": 40, "n": 3, "rules": [{"quote": "If St. Swithin weep, that year, the proverb says, The weather will be foul for forty days.", "cond": {"start": "07-15", "end": "07-15", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "07-15", "end": "08-24", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}}, {"quote": "If St. Swithin greets, the proverb says, The weather will be foul for forty days.", "cond": {"start": "07-15", "end": "07-15", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "07-15", "end": "08-24", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}}, {"quote": "In this month is St. Swithin's Day, on which if that it rain, full forty days after it will some rain distil.", "cond": {"start": "07-15", "end": "07-15", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "07-15", "end": "08-24", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}}]}
{"chunk": 41, "n": 2, "rules": [{"quote": "St. Swithin's Day, if ye do rain, For forty days it will remain", "cond": {"start": "07-15", "end": "07-15", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "07-15", "end": "08-24", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}}, {"quote": "St. Swithin's Day, an ye be fair, For forty days 'twill rain nae mair", "cond": {"start": "07-15", "end": "07-15", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "07-15", "end": "08-24", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}}]}
{"chunk": 42, "n": 1, "rules": [{"quote": "Thunderstorms in the beginning of August will generally be followed by others all the month.", "cond": {"start": "08-01", "end": "08-10", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "08-01", "end": "08-31", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}}]}
{"chunk": 43, "n": 4, "rules": [{"quote": "If the first week in August is unusually warm, the winter will be white and long.", "cond": {"start": "08-01", "end": "08-07", "var": "temp", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "12-01", "end": "02-28", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}}, {"quote": "If on St. Lawrence's Day the weather be fine, fair autumn and good wine may be hoped for.", "cond": {"start": "08-10", "end": "08-10", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "09-01", "end": "11-30", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}}, {"quote": "If this day be misty, the morning beginning with a hoar-frost, the cold weather will soon come, and a hard winter.", "cond": {"start": "08-24", "end": "08-24", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "12-01", "end": "02-28", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}}, {"quote": "If it rains this day, it will rain the forty days after.", "cond": {"start": "08-24", "end": "08-24", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "08-25", "end": "10-03", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}}]}
{"chunk": 44, "n": 3, "rules": [{"quote": "When September has been rainy, the following May is generally dry", "cond": {"start": "09-01", "end": "09-30", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "05-01", "end": "05-31", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}}, {"quote": "When May is dry, the following September is apt to be wet", "cond": {"start": "05-01", "end": "05-31", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "09-01", "end": "09-30", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}}, {"quote": "A wet September, drought for next summer", "cond": {"start": "09-01", "end": "09-30", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "06-01", "end": "08-31", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}}]}
{"chunk": 45, "n": 4, "rules": [{"quote": "If the storms in September clear off warm, all the storms of the following winter will be warm.", "cond": {"start": "09-01", "end": "09-30", "var": "temp", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "12-01", "end": "02-28", "var": "temp", "dir": "above"}}, {"quote": "When a cold spell occurs in September and passes without a frost, a frost will not occur until the same time in October.", "cond": {"start": "09-01", "end": "09-30", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "10-01", "end": "10-31", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}}, {"quote": "Fair on September 1st, fair for the month.", "cond": {"start": "09-01", "end": "09-01", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "09-01", "end": "09-30", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}}, {"quote": "If the hart and the hind meet dry and part dry on Rood Day fair, for sax weeks, of rain there'll be nae mail.", "cond": {"start": "09-14", "end": "09-14", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "09-14", "end": "10-26", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}}]}
{"chunk": 46, "n": 0, "rules": []}
{"chunk": 47, "n": 3, "rules": [{"quote": "If it does not rain on St. Michael's and Gallus, a dry spring is indicated for the next year.", "cond": {"start": "09-29", "end": "10-16", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "03-01", "end": "05-31", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}}, {"quote": "When it freezes and snows in October, January will bring mild weather.", "cond": {"start": "10-01", "end": "10-31", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "01-01", "end": "01-31", "var": "temp", "dir": "above"}}, {"quote": "If October bring heavy frosts and winds, then will January and February be mild.", "cond": {"start": "10-01", "end": "10-31", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "01-01", "end": "02-28", "var": "temp", "dir": "above"}}]}
{"chunk": 48, "n": 2, "rules": [{"quote": "Warm October, cold February.", "cond": {"start": "10-01", "end": "10-31", "var": "temp", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "02-01", "end": "02-28", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}}, {"quote": "If October bring much frost and wind, then are January and February mild.", "cond": {"start": "10-01", "end": "10-31", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "01-01", "end": "02-28", "var": "temp", "dir": "above"}}]}
{"chunk": 49, "n": 3, "rules": [{"quote": "October and November cold indicate that the following January and February will be mild and dry.", "cond": {"start": "10-01", "end": "11-30", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "01-01", "end": "02-28", "var": "temp", "dir": "above"}}, {"quote": "October and November cold indicate that the following January and February will be mild and dry.", "cond": {"start": "10-01", "end": "11-30", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "01-01", "end": "02-28", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}}, {"quote": "If there's ice in November that will bear a duck. There'll be nothing after but sludge and muck.", "cond": {"start": "11-01", "end": "11-30", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "12-01", "end": "02-28", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}}]}
{"chunk": 50, "n": 3, "rules": [{"quote": "Ice in November brings mud in December.", "cond": {"start": "11-01", "end": "11-30", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "12-01", "end": "12-31", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}}, {"quote": "If All Saints' Day will bring out the winter, St. Martin's Day will bring out Indian summer.", "cond": {"start": "11-01", "end": "11-01", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "11-11", "end": "11-11", "var": "temp", "dir": "above"}}, {"quote": "If this day (All Saints') be fair, the next winter will bring but little rain and snow along with it.", "cond": {"start": "11-01", "end": "11-01", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "12-01", "end": "02-28", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}}]}
{"chunk": 51, "n": 2, "rules": [{"quote": "If ducks do swim at Hollantide, At Christmas they will slide.", "cond": {"start": "11-01", "end": "11-01", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "12-25", "end": "12-25", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}}, {"quote": "If the geese at Martin's Day stand on ice, they will walk in mud at Christmas.", "cond": {"start": "11-11", "end": "11-11", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "12-25", "end": "12-25", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}}]}
{"chunk": 52, "n": 2, "rules": [{"quote": "As at Catherine foul or fair, so will be the next February.", "cond": {"start": "11-25", "end": "11-25", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}, "out": {"start": "02-01", "end": "02-28", "var": "precip", "dir": "above"}}, {"quote": "As at Catherine foul or fair, so will be the next February.", "cond": {"start": "11-25", "end": "11-25", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "02-01", "end": "02-28", "var": "precip", "dir": "below"}}]}
{"chunk": 53, "n": 1, "rules": [{"quote": "Frost on the shortest day is said to indicate a severe winter.", "cond": {"start": "12-21", "end": "12-21", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "12-22", "end": "02-28", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}}]}
{"chunk": 54, "n": 1, "rules": [{"quote": "If ice will bear a man before Christmas, it will not bear a mouse afterwards.", "cond": {"start": "12-01", "end": "12-24", "var": "temp", "dir": "below"}, "out": {"start": "12-26", "end": "12-31", "var": "temp", "dir": "above"}}]}
